fact WorkItem(id: "WI-719", description: some(value: "anthill-cli collect_anthill_files sorts ALL collected files GLOBALLY across -p dirs (rustland/anthill-cli/src/main.rs:389 files.sort()), so a project dir that sorts lexicographically BEFORE the stdlib dir (e.g. 'examples/...' < 'stdlib/...', or any absolute path) has its files CONVERTED before stdlib/anthill/prelude/option.anthill registers nil/none/some as constructors. Consequence (the WI-697 nullary-ctor order-dependence, triggered by a real documented usage): structural Option/List patterns in project rules key as Fn{c} while facts key Ref(c) (or vice versa), so they never match — 'anthill query anthill.stage0.workflow.claimable(?id,?desc) --resolve -p stdlib/anthill -p examples/github-todo' returns NO solutions on main even though github_todo_test (which loads stdlib FIRST, then the example) proves the same query resolves to WI-AUTH-001. Also omitted-optional fields in facts converted pre-option.anthill get VAR fills instead of the WI-716 none() fill (observed empirically: ?desc = ?_ duplicates from a scratch -p dir). This silently breaks the documented query workflow in examples/github-todo/rules.anthill's header comment. FIX DIRECTION: either load stdlib-registered files first (sort per -p dir, preserving the -p argument order, mirroring tests' collect order), or robustly: register some/none/nil/cons as constructors in register_prelude (the WI-697 note's 'robust fix'), making conversion order-independent. ACCEPTANCE: the header-comment query above returns WI-AUTH-001 solutions; a -p dir sorting before stdlib gets WI-716 none() fills; cargo-test green. Surfaced verifying WI-717."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-15T06:01:11Z"))
